IMPORT prelude

-- Credit Bureau Act 2016 (Singapore) -- who needs a licence and who may get one (ss 4, 6, 7, 8, 11, 12), what a licensed credit
-- bureau may do with customer information (ss 13, 16), a data subject's copy of his or her credit report (s 17), correcting data
-- (ss 18, 19), approved members and what they may do (ss 27, 29, 33 and First Schedule), and the general penalty and composition
-- (ss 65, 66).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CBA2016.txt, version in force
-- from 9 March 2025, with amendments to Act 5 of 2025 shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions a credit bureau, a
-- lender that uses one, or a person whose credit is reported actually meets. Not encoded: annual fees (s 10), notifications and
-- reports to the Authority (ss 20 to 22), audit (ss 23 to 26), cancellation and revocation of member approval beyond its effect
-- (ss 30 to 32), the duties in ss 34 to 38, control of shareholders and officers (Part 7), inspections (Part 8), the Authority's
-- control of a failing bureau (Part 9), offences by officers (Part 10 save ss 65, 66), appeals procedure (Part 11), the
-- prescribed-entity bar for corporate bureaus (s 13(6)) and anything left to regulations, notices or the Authority's discretion.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Credit Bureau Act 2016 -- credit bureaus`

§§ `4, 6 -- who needs a licence`

-- s 4(1): "this Act does not apply to any public authority", unless the Minister by order declares otherwise (s 4(2)).
-- s 6(1): "a person must not carry on any type of credit reporting business unless the person is licensed by the Authority under
-- this Act in respect of that type of credit reporting business." The licence is by TYPE: consumer, corporate, or both (s 7(2)).
-- s 6(2): an individual -- $125,000 or 3 years or both, plus $12,500 a day continuing; any other person -- $250,000, plus $25,000
-- a day continuing.
DECLARE Licence IS ONE OF
    `no licence`
    `a consumer licence`
    `a corporate licence`
    `a consumer and corporate licence`

DECLARE ReportingType IS ONE OF
    `consumer credit reporting`
    `corporate credit reporting`

GIVEN `the licence held` IS A Licence, `the type` IS A ReportingType
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence covers the type` IF
    CONSIDER `the licence held`
    WHEN `a consumer and corporate licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a consumer licence` THEN `the type` EQUALS `consumer credit reporting`
    WHEN `a corporate licence` THEN `the type` EQUALS `corporate credit reporting`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `is a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister has declared the Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the licence held` IS A Licence, `the type` IS A ReportingType
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carrying on the business is an offence` IF
        ((NOT `is a public authority`) OR `the Minister has declared the Act applies`)
    AND (NOT `the licence covers the type` `the licence held` `the type`)

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlicensed business` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 125000 ELSE 250000

§§ `7, 8 -- getting and renewing a licence`

-- s 7(4): the Authority "must not grant a licence to an applicant unless" (a) "the applicant is a company"; (b) it satisfies the
-- financial and operational requirements; (c) the application comes with the information required and the non-refundable fee.
-- s 7(6): it "must not grant a licence to an applicant to carry on (a) a corporate credit reporting business; or (b) both ...
-- when another person holds a licence for that business." So there can be only one corporate credit bureau; consumer licences
-- are not so limited. INFERENCE: "that business" is read as corporate credit reporting business, so an existing corporate (or
-- consumer and corporate) licensee bars a second applicant for either form that includes corporate reporting.
-- s 7(5): a licence "is valid for 5 years or any shorter period that the Authority may specify".
-- This rule says only whether the Authority MAY grant; whether it does is its discretion (s 7(3)).
GIVEN `the licence sought` IS A Licence, `is a company` IS A BOOLEAN, `meets the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `application is complete with fee` IS A BOOLEAN, `another person holds a corporate licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may grant the licence` IF
        `is a company`
    AND `meets the requirements`
    AND `application is complete with fee`
    AND (NOT (`the licence covers the type` `the licence sought` `corporate credit reporting` AND `another person holds a corporate licence`))

-- s 8(1)(a): a renewal must be made "at least 6 months before the date the licence expires"; (2) if submitted "less than 6 months
-- before the date of expiry", the prescribed late application fee is payable as well.
GIVEN `months before expiry` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a late renewal fee is payable` IF
    `months before expiry` LESS THAN 6

§§ `11, 12 -- losing a licence, and appeal`

-- s 11(2): grounds for revocation include unfit officers or controllers, unsatisfactory finances or conduct, contravention, false
-- information, dishonesty, public interest, failure to pay the annual fee, ceasing business. s 11(4): the Authority "must not
-- revoke ... or suspend ... without giving the licensed credit bureau an opportunity to be heard", except (s 11(5)) where (a) it is
-- being wound up or dissolved; (b) a receiver, judicial manager or equivalent has been appointed; (c) it has been convicted of an
-- offence involving fraud or dishonesty.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `the bureau is being wound up`
    `a receiver has been appointed`
    `a conviction for fraud or dishonesty`
    `unfit officers`
    `failure to pay the annual fee`
    `contravention of the Act`
    `contrary to the public interest`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may act without a hearing` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the bureau is being wound up` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a receiver has been appointed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a conviction for fraud or dishonesty` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 12: a company aggrieved by refusal, revocation or suspension "may, within 30 days after having been informed ... appeal in
-- writing to the Minister". Day 30 is counted as within.
GIVEN `days since informed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence appeal is in time` IF
    `days since informed` AT MOST 30

§§ `13, 16 -- what the bureau may disclose`

-- s 13(2): the bureau "must not disclose any of its members' customer information ... to any person except (a) to an approved
-- member ... where the disclosure is strictly necessary to enable the approved member to assess the creditworthiness of its
-- customer; or (b) to any other person if it is permitted by the Authority by written notice".
-- s 13(5): "Despite subsection (2)", it must not use or disclose customer information where the customer is a public authority, a
-- monetary authority or central bank, or a sovereign wealth fund, or any deposit information.
-- s 13(7): "Despite anything in this section", it may disclose to its own officers solely for its credit reporting business.
-- s 16(1): "Despite section 13", it may disclose customer information or a credit report to (a) the data subject; or (b) a third
-- party "if the licensed credit bureau has the written consent of the data subject".
-- s 13(8): an individual -- $125,000 or 3 years or both; any other person -- $250,000.
--
-- LITERAL READING. s 16 overrides all of s 13, including s 13(5). Read literally, a disclosure to the data subject or with the data
-- subject's written consent is lawful even of deposit information, though s 13(4) forbids collecting it in the first place.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `an approved member assessing its customer's creditworthiness`
    `an approved member for marketing`
    `a lender that is not an approved member`
    `the data subject`
    `a third party with the data subject's written consent`
    `a third party without consent`
    `a person the Authority has permitted by notice`
    `the bureau's own officer for its business`

DECLARE CustomerKind IS ONE OF
    `an individual borrower`
    `a company borrower`
    `a public authority`
    `a central bank`
    `a sovereign wealth fund`

GIVEN `the customer` IS A CustomerKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the customer is protected` IF
    CONSIDER `the customer`
    WHEN `a public authority` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a central bank` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a sovereign wealth fund` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `the customer` IS A CustomerKind, `is deposit information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bureau may disclose the information` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `the data subject` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a third party with the data subject's written consent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the bureau's own officer for its business` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an approved member assessing its customer's creditworthiness` THEN
        (NOT `the customer is protected` `the customer`) AND (NOT `is deposit information`)
    WHEN `a person the Authority has permitted by notice` THEN
        (NOT `the customer is protected` `the customer`) AND (NOT `is deposit information`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for wrongful disclosure` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 125000 ELSE 250000

§§ `17 -- a copy of your own credit report`

-- s 17(1): on a data subject's request the bureau "must, within 5 business days after the request ... provide the data subject
-- with a copy of the credit report". (2) It "may charge the data subject a fee". (3) But where an individual applies for a credit
-- facility from an approved member and requests the report "within 30 days after the approved member has approved or rejected the
-- application", the copy must be provided "free of charge". (4) In one of four forms "at the data subject's option": printed copy
-- collected at the registered office; printed copy by registered post; electronic copy; electronic copy by email.
-- (5) $250,000, plus $25,000 a day continuing.
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `applied for credit from an approved member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days since the application was decided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the copy must be free` IF
        `is an individual`
    AND `applied for credit from an approved member`
    AND `days since the application was decided` AT MOST 30

GIVEN `business days since the request` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bureau is late with the copy` IF
    `business days since the request` GREATER THAN 5

DECLARE Form IS ONE OF
    `a printed copy collected at the registered office`
    `a printed copy by registered post`
    `a printed copy by ordinary post`
    `an electronic copy`
    `an electronic copy by email`
    `a reading over the telephone`

GIVEN `the form` IS A Form
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the data subject may insist on the form` IF
    CONSIDER `the form`
    WHEN `a printed copy by ordinary post` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a reading over the telephone` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `18, 19 -- correcting data`

-- s 18(1): a data subject, and (2) a data provider, may request correction of an error or omission. (3) The bureau must investigate
-- and, "unless it is satisfied on reasonable grounds that a correction should not be made", (i) correct the data and (ii) "send the
-- corrected data to every approved member ... to which the licensed credit bureau disclosed the data within a year before the date
-- the correction was made". A year is taken as 365 days (an assumption; the Act does not count it).
GIVEN `the bureau is satisfied no correction should be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bureau must correct on request` IF
    NOT `the bureau is satisfied no correction should be made`

GIVEN `days between disclosure and correction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member must be sent the corrected data` IF
    `days between disclosure and correction` AT MOST 365

-- s 19(1): the bureau must correct on its own initiative if satisfied there is evidence of a conflict with other information.
-- (2) Except in prescribed circumstances, before correcting it must "(a) inform the data provider ... and (b) subject to
-- subsection (3), obtain consent from that data provider". (3) Consent is not needed "if it is satisfied that any refusal of
-- consent is frivolous or vexatious". Prescribed circumstances are not encoded.
GIVEN `informed the data provider` IS A BOOLEAN, `the data provider consented` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the refusal is frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bureau may make its own correction` IF
        `informed the data provider`
    AND (`the data provider consented` OR `the refusal is frivolous or vexatious`)

§§ `27, 29 and First Schedule -- approved members`

-- s 27: "only an approved member of a licensed credit bureau may receive from the licensed credit bureau customer information".
-- s 29(1): a member within the First Schedule is "deemed to be an approved member ... until that approval is cancelled or
-- revoked". First Schedule: 1. a bank; 2. a merchant bank; 3. a finance company licensed under the Finance Companies Act 1967;
-- 4. a card issuer. Anyone else needs the Authority's approval (s 29(3), (6)).
DECLARE Member IS ONE OF
    `a bank`
    `a merchant bank`
    `a licensed finance company`
    `a card issuer`
    `a moneylender`
    `an insurer`
    `a telecommunications company`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is deemed approved` IF
    CONSIDER `the member`
    WHEN `a moneylender` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an insurer` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a telecommunications company` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member, `approved by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `approval cancelled or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member may receive customer information` IF
        (`the member is deemed approved` `the member` OR `approved by the Authority`)
    AND (NOT `approval cancelled or revoked`)

-- s 33(1), (2): an approved member must not request or use customer information from the bureau except "(a) where the customer
-- information is strictly necessary to assess the creditworthiness of a customer of the approved member; or (b) any other purpose
-- that the Authority may permit, by written notice".
-- s 33(5): it must not disclose customer information to the bureau if the bureau's licence "(a) has lapsed; (b) is revoked; or
-- (c) is suspended"; s 33(7): it must never disclose its deposit information to the bureau.
-- s 33(9): an individual -- $125,000 or 3 years or both; any other person -- $250,000.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `assessing a customer's creditworthiness`
    `marketing other products`
    `screening a job applicant`
    `a purpose the Authority has permitted`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member may request or use the information` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `assessing a customer's creditworthiness` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a purpose the Authority has permitted` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `is deposit information` IS A BOOLEAN, `the bureau's licence has lapsed, been revoked or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the purpose is permitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member may disclose to the bureau` IF
        `the purpose is permitted`
    AND (NOT `is deposit information`)
    AND (NOT `the bureau's licence has lapsed, been revoked or suspended`)

§§ `65, 66 -- general penalty and composition`

-- s 65: where no penalty is expressly provided, "(a) in the case of an individual, to a fine not exceeding $50,000; or (b) in any
-- other case, to a fine not exceeding $100,000". (So the s 29(11), 30(9) and 31(10) offences of a bureau, which state no penalty,
-- carry $100,000.)
-- s 66(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum of money not exceeding half of the amount of the maximum
-- fine prescribed for that offence". Which offences are prescribed is not in the Act.
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the general maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 50000 ELSE 100000

GIVEN `the maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound` MEANS
    `the maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2
